# Positioning (E5, docs/desktop/WEBVIEWER_ENGINE.md#positioning), block
# geometry only: a relative box that moves without moving the next one; in a
# relative containing block (padding box 420x220), absolute boxes placed by
# top and left, by right and bottom, stretched by all four, centred by auto
# margins, sized in percentages, at their static position, shrunk to fit, and
# sized by their content upwards from the bottom; an absolute box in the
# viewport, a fixed one, and the painting order of z-index -1, auto and 2.
# Laid out at 800 by 585, the room Chromium leaves under its horizontal
# scroll bar here; every box matches its getBoundingClientRect.
viewport 800 585
paint
block html 0 0 800 331
  block body 8 8 784 315
    block div relative 28 18 784 30
    block div 8 38 784 20
    block div relative 8 73 430 230
      anonymous 23 88 400 0
        block div absolute 13 78 50 40
        block div absolute 359 244 64 34
        block div absolute 43 128 350 110
        block div absolute 173 83 100 10
        block div absolute 55 133 210 22
      block div 23 88 400 25
      anonymous 23 113 400 0
        block div absolute 23 113 30 30
        block div absolute 355 178 78 20
          block div 359 182 70 12
        block div absolute 213 265 20 33
          block div 213 265 20 33
    anonymous 8 303 784 0
      block div absolute 720 545 80 40
      block div fixed 600 10 100 20
    block div relative 8 303 784 10
    block div 8 313 784 10
      block div absolute 0 0 10 10
paint block html 0 0
paint block div 0 0
paint block body 8 8
paint block div 8 38
paint block anonymous 8 303
paint block div 8 313
paint block div 28 18
paint block div 8 73
paint block anonymous 23 88
paint block div 23 88
paint block anonymous 23 113
paint block div 13 78
paint block div 359 244
